          %h2#references References
          %h3#axioms_2 Axioms
          %p
            The original article that introduced the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haag-Kastler+axioms"} Haag-Kastler axioms
            is
          %ul
            %li#Haag64
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"}> Rudolf Haag
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kastler"} Daniel Kastler
              = succeed "," do
                %em An algebraic approach to quantum field theory
              %strong 5
              (1964) 848-861 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1704187"}> doi:10.1063/1.1704187
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/9124"} spire:9124
          %p following
          %ul
            %li#Haag59
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"}> Rudolf Haag
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Discussion des “axiomes” et des propriétés asymptotiques d’une théorie des champs locales avec particules composées, Les Problèmes Mathématiques de la Théorie Quantique des Champs
          %p translated to English as:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"}> Rudolf Haag
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Discussion of the ‘axioms’ and the asymptotic properties of a local field theory with composite particles
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1140/epjh/e2010-10041-3"} doi:10.1140/epjh/e2010-10041-3
          %p
            The generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            from open in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
            to more general and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curved
            spacetimes (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"} AQFT on curved spacetimes
          %ul
            %li#BrunettiFredenhagen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                %em Quantum field theory on curved spacetimes
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0901.2063"} arXiv:0901.2063
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Verch"} Rainer Verch
                %em The generally covariant locality principle – A new paradigm for local quantum physics
                Commun. Math. Phys. 237:31-68 (2003) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0112041"}> arXiv:math-ph/0112041
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                %em Quantum Field Theory on Curved Backgrounds
                , Proceedings of the Kompaktkurs “Quantenfeldtheorie auf gekruemmten Raumzeiten” held at Universitaet Potsdam, Germany, in 8.-12.10.2007, organized by C. Baer and K. Fredenhagen
          %p
            See also
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"} AQFT on curved spacetimes
            \.
          %h3#lecture_notes_and_textbooks Lecture notes and Textbooks
          %p Introductory lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Garth+Warner"}> Garth Warner
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Field Theory Seminar (School of Haag-Kastler et al.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://sites.math.washington.edu//~warner/QFT2Seminar_Warner.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Warner-HaagKastlerQFT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Fredenhagen03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"}> Klaus Fredenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraische Quantenfeldtheorie
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FredenhagenAQFT2003.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#FewsterRejzner19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Fewster"}> Christopher Fewster
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"} Kasia Rejzner
                %em Algebraic Quantum Field Theory - an introduction
                (
